<task id="012" project="spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-08: requestType match key on RoutingContext/IRoutingContext + keyed intake harness contract and registry (unknown key → triage)</title>
    <phase>1 Pipeline core and first doors</phase>
    <gate>after 005 (shared files)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies a PublicContracts interface used across the BFF and adds new .cs abstractions and DI registrations (bff-api).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>New abstraction authoring (the harness contract every future harness implements) plus a non-breaking change to a cross-cutting routing contract; the Binding-to-harness mapping needs judgment.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P1-A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>005</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, ai, di, unit-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add a `RequestType` routing dimension to `IRoutingContext`/`RoutingContext` without breaking existing implementers or Bindings, teach `ConsumerRoutingService` to match the `"requestType"` key, and add an intake harness contract plus a DI-keyed harness registry (pattern: ToolHandlerRegistry / NodeExecutorRegistry) that resolves a harness for a request type + document type, returning a "no harness" result (→ manual triage) instead of throwing.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the AI consumer-routing contract (Bindings, match conditions, ConsumerTypes) and .NET DI registries. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>`IRoutingContext.RequestType` (default-implemented, returns null) and `RoutingContext.RequestType`; `ConsumerRoutingService.ResolveContextValue` maps `"requestType"`; `IIntakeHarness` (key, CanHandle, Run returning documents, results, approval-required flag, return payload, persist hook) and `IntakeHarnessRegistry` (built from `IEnumerable&lt;IIntakeHarness&gt;`, case-insensitive, duplicate keys fail at startup); a `ConsumerTypes.IntakeHarness` Binding consumer type whose match conditions carry `requestType`; unit tests for all of it. No harness is implemented here (NDA harness = task 015).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-08 (acceptance a–d), FR-10 (no harness → triage), project CLAUDE.md §2 ("RoutingContext carries only MimeType and DocumentType today"). `IRoutingContext` at `IConsumerRoutingService.cs:341`, `RoutingContext` at `:364`; match-key switch at `ConsumerRoutingService.cs:1201-1213` (unknown key → no match). The harness contract shape is from spec FR-08 ("takes request, run and content, and returns documents, results, an approval-required flag, a return payload and a persist hook"); "content" means references (document ids / staged blob paths), never bytes in memory beyond what a harness reads. Mapping a Binding to a harness: the Binding resolved for `intake-harness` with `{"requestType": "nda"}` must name the harness key using an EXISTING Binding field (candidates in `Binding.cs`: `ConsumerCode`, `WorkflowClass`); record the choice in notes.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IConsumerRoutingService.cs (:341 IRoutingContext, :364 RoutingContext)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ConsumerRoutingService.cs (:1201-1213 ResolveContextValue)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ConsumerTypes.cs (IntakeHarness + All)</file>
      <file role="modify">infra/dataverse/sprk_playbookconsumer-rows.json (one `intake-harness` Binding row, requestType = nda)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/JobProcessingModule.cs (register the registry)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Intake/Harnesses/IIntakeHarness.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Intake/Harnesses/IntakeHarnessContracts.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Intake/Harnesses/IntakeHarnessRegistry.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/domain/Intake/IntakeHarnessRegistryTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ConsumerRoutingServiceContextFilterTests.cs (requestType cases)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/ToolHandlerRegistry.cs:27 and src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Nodes/NodeExecutorRegistry.cs:29</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/Binding.cs (existing fields; no new Binding column)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="005" status="pending">005 edits ConsumerTypes.cs and JobProcessingModule.cs (file overlap). Task 004 also appends to ConsumerTypes.cs and sprk_playbookconsumer-rows.json: rebase on it if it merged first (append-only, different entries). Task 013 consumes the registry; 015 adds the NDA harness.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">Scope: IRoutingContext. The new member is a default interface member returning null so no existing implementer or caller changes; every existing routing test passes unchanged (FR-08b).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Scope: RequestType. A deterministic identifier (e.g. `nda`), never user text, matching the interface's existing ADR-015 remark.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">Scope: the new consumer type. `ConsumerTypes.IntakeHarness`, its `All` entry and its Binding row land in the same change; `/healthz/catalog` reports no drift.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Scope: DI. Register the registry as a concrete singleton/scoped per the ToolHandlerRegistry precedent; `IIntakeHarness` is a real seam (multiple implementations); no other new interfaces.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the registry. An unknown or unregistered request type returns an explicit "no harness" result that the orchestrator maps to manual triage (FR-08c, FR-10); it never throws for that case. Duplicate harness keys fail at construction.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: Binding schema. No new Binding/`sprk_playbookconsumer` column; the harness key rides an existing Binding field.</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions">Scope: the PR. State the Placement Justification (`.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`), measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master build, ≤ 60 MB total, no new HIGH CVE; update the CAPABILITY-INDEX row if the registry becomes a canonical component (main session applies `.claude/` edits).</constraint>
  </constraints>

