      <pattern name="Keyed handler registry" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/ToolHandlerRegistry.cs">Constructor takes IEnumerable of handlers, builds a case-insensitive dictionary, logs registered keys.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Match-key resolution" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ConsumerRoutingService.cs">`ResolveContextValue` switch: add `"requestType" => context.RequestType`.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Add `RequestType` to IRoutingContext (default member) and RoutingContext; add the `"requestType"` case to ResolveContextValue; extend ConsumerRoutingServiceContextFilterTests.</step>
    <step order="2">Define the harness contract (IIntakeHarness + request/result records) from spec FR-08; results carry ids and references only.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement IntakeHarnessRegistry (resolve by harness key from the Binding; "no harness" result for null/unknown); register in JobProcessingModule.</step>
    <step order="4">Add `ConsumerTypes.IntakeHarness`, its `All` entry and one Binding row (`requestType` = `nda`, harness key `nda` in the chosen existing Binding field).</step>
    <step order="5">Write IntakeHarnessRegistryTests (resolve, unknown → no-harness, duplicate key → startup failure, case-insensitive) and run RoutingConsumerTypeHealthCheckTests.</step>
    <step order="6">`dotnet build`, `dotnet test`; measure publish size vs fresh master.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="8">Record the Binding-field choice and any deviation in `projects/spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If naming the harness key on a Binding needs a new `sprk_playbookconsumer` column or repurposes a field with existing semantics that other code reads, STOP and escalate per root CLAUDE.md §6 with the options.</trigger>
    <trigger>If adding `RequestType` would break a public contract (an implementer outside the BFF, a serialized shape, an MCP schema), STOP and escalate (breaking API contract, root CLAUDE.md §6).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>reuse-scan.md row 3 (routing key: `IConsumerRoutingService.cs:364`, extend) and row 2 (keyed registry: `ToolHandlerRegistry.cs:27`, `NodeExecutorRegistry.cs:29` — "new registry, pattern copied"); CAPABILITY-INDEX row 16 (AI analysis / node executors) covers other concepts.</existing>
    <extension>RequestType: Yes — extends `RoutingContext`/`IRoutingContext`. Registry: No — the existing registries key node executors and tools, not request work; the harness contract has different inputs and outputs (spec §11 row "Harness contract and registry").</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The orchestrator cannot route a request by type, so every request type would need its own pipeline and an unknown type would have no triage path (FR-08a, FR-08c, FR-10 fail).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
