  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a Binding with match condition `{"requestType":"nda"}` and a RoutingContext with RequestType `nda`, routing resolves that Binding and the registry returns the harness registered under its key (FR-08a, with a test harness).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All existing ConsumerRoutingService and routing tests pass unchanged; contexts without RequestType route exactly as before (FR-08b).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a request type with no Binding, or a Binding whose key has no registered harness, yields the "no harness" result — no exception (FR-08c).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: two harnesses with the same key make registry construction fail with a clear message.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Adding a harness needs only a harness class, one DI line and one Binding row (FR-08d) — demonstrated by the test harness setup.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`ConsumerTypes.All` includes `intake-harness`; RoutingConsumerTypeHealthCheckTests report no drift; DiGraphValidationTests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">PR states Placement Justification and publish-size delta (≤ 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes. All tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>`Services/Intake/` is a proposed new folder for all intake pipeline BFF code (orchestrator 013, dispatch 014, harnesses 015, triage 016); keep it unless the BFF CLAUDE.md names a better home.</notes>

